{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated code generation pipeline (cobbler-scaffold) and has assigned task #5659: implement `cmd/pr/main.go` for the GNU `pr` utility (paginate or columnate files for printing). The specific requirements to implement are from srd110-pr.yaml:\n   - **R3.1**: Multi-column output (`-COLUMN`, `--columns=COLUMN`, `-a`/`--across` for fill direction)\n   - **R4.1**: Line numbering (`-n[CHAR[WIDTH]]`, `--number-lines[=CHAR[WIDTH]]`, default separator tab, default width 5)\n   - **R4.2**: Indent and width (`-o MARGIN`/`--indent=MARGIN`, `-w WIDTH`/`--width=WIDTH` default 72)\n   - **R4.3**: Double-space (`-d`/`--double-space`) and column separator (`-s CHAR`/`--separator=CHAR` default tab)\n   \n   The file to create is `cmd/pr/main.go`. The binary must compile with `go build -o bin/pr ./cmd/pr/`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU `pr` utility: paginates text files with headers, footers, page numbers, multi-column layout\n   - Page layout: 66 lines default (5 header, 56 body, 5 footer), header shows date/filename/page number\n   - Multi-column: columns filled down by default, `-a` fills across\n   - Line numbering with configurable separator char and width\n   - Page width default 72, configurable indent margin\n   - Double-spacing and column separator configuration\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing against `gpr` (Homebrew GNU coreutils)\n   - Non-goal: `-m` (merge files side by side) is NOT implemented in this release\n   - Exit codes: 0 on success, 1 on error\n   - Go module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - 40-line function limit (hard), 500-line file limit\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd110-pr.yaml** (READ)\n     - Contains full SRD for pr utility with requirements R1-R5\n     - Key requirements for this task: R3.1 (multi-column), R4.1 (line numbering), R4.2 (indent/width), R4.3 (double-space/separator)\n     - Supporting requirements needed: R1.1 (page layout), R2.1-R2.3 (page options), R5.1-R5.2 (exit codes, SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: `-m` (merge files) not implemented\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n     - Full content read and available above in the conversation\n   \n   - **cmd/pr/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Main implementation file for the pr utility\n     - Must implement R3.1, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3 (and supporting R1, R2, R5 infrastructure)\n   \n   - Reference files listed in required_reading (NOT yet read, contents in repository):\n     - `cmd/nl/main.go` - reference for line numbering and section handling\n     - `cmd/fmt/main.go` - reference for paragraph reformatting\n     - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` - SIGPIPE handler pattern\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one read operation was performed before the summary request.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand all requirements. The task specifies R3.1, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3 but a functional utility requires implementing the full page layout (R1), page options (R2), and exit/signal handling (R5) as supporting infrastructure. The implementation needs to handle:\n     - Page layout with configurable length, header/footer\n     - Multi-column output with down-fill and across-fill modes\n     - Line numbering with configurable separator and width\n     - Indent margin and page width\n     - Double-spacing and column separators\n     - File reading from args or stdin\n     - Proper exit codes and SIGPIPE\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task description with full project context, execution constitution, go style guide, task specification for implementing cmd/pr with requirements R3.1, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3 from srd110-pr.yaml\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/pr/main.go` implementing R3.1, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3 (plus supporting R1, R2, R5)\n   - Read reference implementations (`cmd/nl/main.go`, `cmd/fmt/main.go`) for patterns\n   - Build and verify: `go build -o bin/pr ./cmd/pr/`\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/pr/`\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria AC1-AC6\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd110-pr.yaml`) to understand the requirements. I was about to read reference implementations (`cmd/nl/main.go`, `cmd/fmt/main.go`) and then implement the `cmd/pr/main.go` file. No code has been written yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read the reference implementations (`cmd/nl/main.go` and `cmd/fmt/main.go`) to understand patterns for line numbering and text formatting, then implement `cmd/pr/main.go` covering:\n   - Page layout (R1.1): 66-line pages with 5-line header (date, filename, page number), 56-line body, 5-line footer\n   - Page options (R2.1-R2.3): `-l`, `-h`, `-t`, `-T`, stdin/file reading\n   - Multi-column (R3.1): `-COLUMN`/`--columns=COLUMN`, `-a`/`--across`\n   - Formatting (R4.1-R4.3): `-n` line numbering, `-o` indent, `-w` width, `-d` double-space, `-s` separator\n   - Exit/signal (R5.1-R5.2): exit codes and SIGPIPE handler\n   \n   The task description states: \"files: path: cmd/pr/main.go, action: create, note: pr utility implementation covering SRD requirements R3.1, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go